Generate official source URLs
The NHANES public-use files in this tutorial follow this structure:
https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/
{cycle_start}/DataFiles/{file_id}.xpt
Create a URL function:
build_nhanes_url &lt;- function(
    cycle_start,
    file_id) {

  if (
    length(cycle_start) != 1 ||
    is.na(cycle_start)
  ) {
    stop(
      "cycle_start must contain one nonmissing value."
    )
  }

  if (
    length(file_id) != 1 ||
    is.na(file_id) ||
    !nzchar(file_id)
  ) {
    stop(
      "file_id must contain one nonempty value."
    )
  }

  paste0(
    "https://wwwn.cdc.gov/",
    "Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/",
    cycle_start,
    "/DataFiles/",
    file_id,
    ".xpt"
  )
}
Test it:
build_nhanes_url(
  cycle_start = 2017,
  file_id = "CBC_J"
)
Expected result:
https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/CBC_J.xpt

Populate every catalog URL
Run:
nhanes_catalog &lt;- nhanes_catalog |&gt;
  dplyr::mutate(
    url = purrr::map2_chr(
      cycle_start,
      file_id,
      build_nhanes_url
    )
  )
Inspect:
nhanes_catalog |&gt;
  dplyr::select(
    dataset_id,
